    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d549">

                <pb facs="0071" n="1271" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v07p2/pg1271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762A.6/6–2452: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 549<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Department of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d549-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-06-24T18:00:00+01:00">June 24, 1952—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 3. Secy and Eden this morn agreed on desirability of 12 month staggered
                    stockpile in Berlin to be worked out so far as possible between HICOMs and Gers. It was also agreed that
                    simplification of command structure and retaliatory counter should be worked out
                    by HICOMs, in the latter case so far as
                    possible with the Gers, so as to be ready to put them into effect in the event
                    of blockade. Agreed also common survey airlift possibilities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d549-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d549-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary Acheson was in London to receive
                    an honorary degree from Oxford University and as the first step in a trip that
                    also included visits to Berlin, Vienna, and Rio de Janeiro. Regarding his visit
                    to Berlin, see telegram 1375, <ref target="#d551">Document 551</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
